    {"Hay - raking loss", "Grass, alfalfa", "0.02 (1 + 2 fl)(1 - m)^1.5 / Ds", "Rotz 1995, Trans. ASAE 38(6):1621, Eq. 13"},
    {"Hay - baler loss", "Grass, alfalfa", "Pickup 0.003 / (m Ds); chamber 0.0025 fb m^-1.2, fb 1.0 small square (0.5 at night), 0.5 midsize/large square, 1.0 variable round, 2.5 fixed round; Ds = windrow density, windrow as wide as the baler pickup", "Rotz 1995, Trans. ASAE 38(6):1621, Eq. 12 and 14; K-State MF2834 (windrow 1/2 to full pickup width)"},
    {"Hay - bale storage", "Grass, alfalfa", "First month by baling moisture: 12 % 0.5, 15 % 1.5, 18 % 2.6, 20 % 3.4, 25 % 5.7, 30 % 8.6 %; then 0.3 % a month; wrapped bales stop", "USDA-ARS IFSM Reference Manual ch. 7, Eq. 7.1-7.4 (Buckmaster et al. 1989b)"},
    {"Regrowth after a cut", "Alfalfa, grass", "Alfalfa harvest ready 1 month after a cut (35 days); grass 2 months (60 days); growing season only", "UC IPM (UC ANR) Alfalfa Harvest: 26-35 day intervals; Penn State Extension, Timing Second Cutting Grass Hay (2025): 30-60 days"},
    {"Winter - snow on the ground", "Timothy", "Snow if the high is below 1 C; 10 cm per 10 mm; melts 1 cm per C above 1 C and 4 cm per 10 mm of rain", "Ritchie 1991, as given in Kanneganti, Rotz & Walgenbach 1998, Agron. J. 90:687"},
    {"Winter - which numbers each state uses", "Alfalfa, grass", "Same rule on every map. The model where it matched USDA within 1 point or 2 times; USDA's own year-by-year numbers where it did not; the game weather is never changed", "Team rule 2026-11-04; check table in the project doc cfa-winter-state-table"},
    {"Winter - 4-inch soil low", "Alfalfa", "The real winter at the nearest NOAA soil station whose coldest air low is closest to the game winter's", "NOAA GHCN-Daily soil temp (10 cm) and NOAA USCRN hourly soil temp (10 cm), 63 stations"},
    {"Winter - alfalfa first winter (model)", "Alfalfa", "Dies only if 4-inch soil reaches 15 F; then 0/0/45/40 % at -10.5/-12.3/-13.2/-15.9 C (high end at or warmer)", "Iowa State Extension (Lang & Vittetoe 2019; Michel 2023); Leep, Andresen & Jeranyama 2001, Agron. J. 93:1142, Vernal, fall-seeded plots"},
    {"Winter - USDA years", "Alfalfa, grass", "% of insured acres with a Cold Winter, Freeze or Frost loss (Nov-Apr), by state and year; the year matched to how cold the game winter was", "USDA RMA Cause of Loss + Summary of Business 2005-2025; Forage Seeding (first winter), Forage Production (established)"},
    {"Winter - alfalfa stand to yield", "Alfalfa", "Starts at 160 plants/m2; percent of potential yield by plants per sq ft and stand age; this year's loss = % last fall - % now", "Kanneganti et al. 1998 (Wisconsin average); Michigan State Extension E-2310 (Hesterman & Durling 1991), Table 3 and Example 2"},
    {"Winter - grass (timothy)", "Grass", "Surface temp = air x e^(-65 x snow m); hardening to -26.7 C; tillers die 1 - 1/(1+e^(surface - hardiness)) per day, max 50 %; tillers killed come off the yield", "BASGRA_2014 (Van Oijen, Hoglind, Cameron, Thorsen), Zenodo 27867, timothy; FS25 grass = timothy (team, from the game's grass texture)"},
    {"Insurance - alfalfa and grass", "Alfalfa, grass", "Forage Production, APH 50-75 %, one policy year per field (first growth of the game year is covered and charged); covers adverse weather incl. winterkill", "USDA RMA Summary of Business 2021-2025, South Dakota (most insured acres); Forage Production Crop Provisions 27-0033"},
    {"Alfalfa - cutting order", "Alfalfa", "Yield of each cutting vs the year's best: 1st 100 %, 2nd 100 %, 3rd 90.8 %, 4th 68.3 %, 5th and later 65.3 % (high end of each position); not insured", "Djaman, Owen, Koudahe & O'Neill 2020, Agronomy 10:136 (NMSU); Xu, Min & McDonald 2021, J. Anim. Sci. Technol. 63:1098, Table 4 (Kansas State)"},
    {"Alfalfa - late fall cut", "Alfalfa", "Last cut 14+ days before the station's median first 28 F freeze: no effect; 1 day after or later: -14.9 % yield the next year; straight line between; not insured", "McDonald, Min & Baral 2021, J. Anim. Sci. Technol. 63:799, Table 6 (Kansas State, Manhattan); NOAA U.S. Climate Normals 1991-2020, median first 28 F freeze (Manhattan USC00144972: Oct 29; each station's own)"},
    {"Alfalfa - late fall cut (other research)", "Alfalfa", "Research disagrees: irrigated Utah found the damage 2-6 weeks BEFORE the mean killing frost and none after it. CFA keeps Kansas (rain-fed, closer to our farms); this row has no effect", "Horrocks & Zarifnejad 1997, J. Prod. Agric. 10:96 (Brigham Young Univ., Spanish Fork UT)"},
    {"Where the numbers come from", "Whole mod", "Built from U.S. sources (NOAA, USDA, U.S. Extension, peer-reviewed papers), Canadian sources (Environment and Climate Change Canada) and European sources (Poland IMGW and Ministry of Agriculture; Germany DWD, GDV, Vereinigte Hagel; UK Met Office; Met Eireann; Meteo-France, CCR). Each row on this tab names its own source. Insurance in Europe uses that country's own numbers, not USDA", "Each row below"},
    {"Daily normals - Canada and Europe", "Crops already growing when CFA first sees them", "One normal high / low per calendar day, 1991-2020, for 899 stations (84 Canada, 815 Europe). NOAA's method: 6-harmonic fit to each day's 30-year average, each month averaging exactly to the monthly normal. Check on 3 U.S. stations vs NOAA official: within 0.7 F, corn degree days within 1.5 %", "Arguez et al. 2012 (NOAA NCEI Daily Temperature Normals Methodology); NOAA GHCN-Daily (ECCC), IMGW, DWD, Met Office MIDAS, Met Eireann, Meteo-France"},
    {"Planting dates - Germany", "Corn and silage corn 4/27, winter wheat 10/9, winter barley 9/24, spring barley 3/28, oats 3/28, winter rye 10/1, sugar beet 4/4, sunflower 4/20", "Start of sowing at each DWD reporting station; median of all reports per year, averaged over the last 5 full years (2019-2023; sunflower 2012, 2013, 2021-2023 - years with 30+ reports). Canola left out: CFA's canola is spring canola, Germany sows winter rape", "DWD Climate Data Center, phenology annual reporters, crops (CC BY 4.0)"},
    {"Planting dates - France", "Corn and silage corn 4/27, soft (winter) wheat 10/26, winter barley 10/19, spring barley 3/2", "National 5-year average 2021-2025, first week ending at or above 50 % sown - the same rule as USDA NASS. Oats, rye, sugar beet, sunflower: not in Cere'Obs, so no date", "FranceAgriMer Cere'Obs weekly crop progress reports (2026 reports, Moyenne 2021-2025 column)"},
    {"Planting dates - Canada", "Alberta May 19, Saskatchewan May 18, Manitoba May 26 - spring wheat, barley, oats, canola, flax, peas, lentils, chickpeas, mustard, soybeans, corn", "One date per province (team): the provinces publish a 5-year average (2021-2025) for all crops together, not per crop. First week at or above 50 % seeded (USDA rule): AB 61 % (31 % a week before), SK 55 % (28 %), MB 68 % (43 %). Ontario, Quebec and fall-sown crops: no date yet. In Aug-Feb a crop that may be fall-sown is not rebuilt without a fall date", "Alberta Crop Report (week ended May 19 2026); Saskatchewan Crop Report No. 3, May 12-18 2026; Manitoba Crop Report May 26 2026, Figure 1"},
    {"Planting dates - Poland", "Corn and silage corn 4/29, spring wheat 3/27, spring barley 3/29, oats 3/28, winter wheat 10/5, winter barley 9/25, winter rye 9/28, winter triticale 10/1", "Mean sowing date of all trial sites in Poland's official post-registration variety trials, averaged over harvest years 2021-2025 (corn 2020-2024). Poland has no weekly sowing survey, so trial sowing dates are used", "COBORU, Wyniki Porejestrowych Doswiadczen Odmianowych (zboza jare, zboza ozime, kukurydza) 2021-2025, tables Warunki prowadzenia doswiadczen"},
    {"Planting dates - Great Britain", "England, Scotland, Wales: winter wheat 10/10, winter barley 9/26", "Share of the crop drilled in September, October and November; 50 % point with drilling spread evenly through the month; mean of autumns 2021, 2022, 2024, 2025 (the 2023 report gave no split). Spring crops and Northern Ireland: no date yet", "AHDB Arable Crop Condition Reports, November 2021, 2022, 2024, 2025 (RSK ADAS for AHDB)"},
    {"Planting dates - Ireland", "Winter wheat 10/15, winter barley 10/5, spring barley 3/23", "Ireland has no sowing survey, so Teagasc's advice is used (team): middle of each advised window. Advice, not a measured average", "Teagasc via Agriland (mid-October for winter wheat); Teagasc, Hold your horses on sowing winter barley (2024): late September to mid-October; Teagasc Spring Barley Guide: sown 10 March - 4 April"},
    {"Planting dates - Quebec", "Corn 5/15, soybeans 5/22, oats 5/11, barley 5/12, spring wheat 5/8", "Mean sowing date of Quebec's official variety-trial sites, years 2021, 2022, 2023 and 2025 (the 2024 report was not found). Same method as Poland", "RGCQ / CEROM Guide des reseaux d'essais 2021, 2022, 2023; La Terre de chez nous RGCQ results 2025 (corn, oleaginous, cereals)"},
    {"Planting dates - Ontario", "Corn 5/3, soybeans 5/1; spring wheat, barley, oats 4/10 southwest, 4/15 central and east, 5/10 north", "No measured average, so government advice is used (team), middle of each window. Regions: north = 46 N and up, southwest = west of 81 W, rest = central and east", "OMAFA Field Crop News (corn: late April to the first half of May); Grain Farmers of Ontario / University of Guelph 2025 (soybeans: late April or early May); OMAFRA Agronomy Guide Pub. 811 ch. 4 (spring cereal target dates)"},
    {"Planting dates - other countries", "Northern Ireland; UK spring crops; Irish crops other than wheat and barley", "No sourced national planting date yet, so a crop already growing on a new save starts its clock the day CFA first sees it (Rule #1)", "Team 2026-11-15"},
    {"Silage - chopping moisture", "Grass, alfalfa (windrow), corn", "Shown while chopping. Bunker target 65-70 % moisture; warning over 70 % (leaks, spoils) and under 40 % (heats, fire risk). No yield loss (no sourced loss curve)", "Penn State Extension, From Harvest to Feed: Understanding Silage Management, Table 4; Oregon State Forage Information System, Silage"},
    {"Silage - corn moisture", "Corn chopped with a forage harvester", "73 % whole-plant moisture at dent (R5), drying 0.75 points a day (high end of 0.50-0.75). Milk line not used: heat units from dent to maturity disagree between K-State, Purdue, UW and Iowa State", "Penn State Extension, Corn Silage Production and Management, Table 3 and drydown"},
    {"Silage - corn chopped early", "Corn chopped with a forage harvester", "Yield kept by moisture: 73 % 87.4 %, 66 % 98.4 %, 63 % 100 %, 60 % and drier 98.4 % (16.0 / 18.0 / 18.3 / 18.0 t/A); straight line between. Grain harvest not affected", "Penn State Extension, Corn Silage Production and Management, Table 3"},
    {"Silage - feed-out face", "Opened bunker silos", "Share spoiled at the face by how fast it moves: 0.18 m/wk 18 %, 0.53 6 %, 1.07 3 %, 2.14 1.5 % (641 kg/m3, Penn State ideal bunker density). Speed = face meters taken over the last game month / weeks in it (game month = real month)", "Holmes & Muck 2007, in Borreani et al. 2018, J. Dairy Sci. 101:3952, Fig. 13; Penn State (40 lb/ft3)"},
    {"Silage - safe feed-out speed", "Opened bunker silos (notice only)", "Minimum face speed = 0.0014 T^2 + 0.0133 T + 1.079 m/wk, T = station's normal mean temperature for the season (Nov-Mar, May-Sep; April and October their own month)", "Borreani & Tabacco 2012, in Borreani et al. 2018, Fig. 15 and Table 6"},
    {"Un-cured bales", "Grass, alfalfa", "Wet windrow does not dry in the bale. Up to 34 % moisture: stored like tough hay, hay losses apply. Over 34 %: no effect, wrap within 24 h for baleage (40-55 %)", "Wilcke, Cuomo & Fox 1999 (U of MN); UMN Extension Wrapping hay; UGA B1508"},
    {"Peanut freeze (grade)", "Peanut", "Dug peanuts in the windrow at 32 F or colder within 96 h of digging, or dug the day after a freeze: Seg 2 grade, 35 % of value (taken as fewer peanuts picked)", "NC State, Digging Date and Freeze Damage (Jordan 2024); NC State Peanut Info 2023; USDA FSA 2014 Seg 2 loan rate"},
    {"Canola frost after flowering", "Canola", "29 F or colder from late flower to early ripening (seed still filling, over 40 % moisture): seed killed, 100 % loss. Frost at flowering: minor, no effect", "NDSU, Effect of Frost on Flowering Canola; NDSU A686 Canola Production; K-State MF3236"},
    {"Fall-sown barley freeze", "Barley (sown Aug-Feb)", "Heading 166 days, seed fill 177 days after planting; spring freeze rows (24.8 F 50 %, 21.2 F 77 %) from heading to seed fill", "USDA-ARS 2003-04 Uniform Winter Barley Trial (Kinston NC); NDAWN 319 GDD at NOAA Goldsboro NC normals"},
    {"Black beans (dry beans)", "Black bean", "Growth clock 50/86 F; stages R1 40 to R9 94 days; drought Ky 1.15; hail ND 2.4 %/yr, 50.5 % on hit; wind 0.8 %/yr, 27.9 %. Frost below 30 F from R2 to R8 (pods green): 100 %", "NDSU A1133, Berglund 2021; OMAFRA Pub 811; HPRCC AWDN; FAO-56 Tables 11, 12, 22, 24; USDA RMA Cause of Loss + NASS ND 2001-2025"},
    {"Alfalfa - cutting interval", "Alfalfa", "No rule: only a 20-day interval hurt the stand (54 % survival vs 83-85 % at 30-40 days); alfalfa regrows in one month in the game", "Ventroni, Volenec & Cangiano 2010, Field Crops Research 119:252, Table 4"},
    {"Alfalfa rotation tip", "Alfalfa", "Most growers rotate after the seeding year plus 2-3 production years", "University of Minnesota Extension, Managing the rotation from alfalfa to corn (Yost, Coulter & Russelle)"},
    {"Insurance - premiums", "15 crops (lead state)", "Liability, total premium, farmer-paid premium per acre, 50-85 % coverage; YP, RP, RP-HPE, APH", "USDA RMA Summary of Business by coverage level, 2021-2025"},
    {"Insurance - rules", "All insured crops", "Policy per crop, renews until cancelled; attaches at planting; premium due when coverage begins; buy before planting", "USDA RMA Insurance Cycle; Center for Rural Affairs, Crop Insurance 101"},
    {"Insurance - revenue plans", "RP, RP-HPE", "RP: guarantee at higher of projected or harvest price, harvest price at most 2.00 x projected; RP-HPE: projected price only, harvest price capped at projected", "RMA Commodity Exchange Price Provisions Sec. I 2(f); ProAg RP / RP-HPE plan pages"},
    {"Game - rolling", "All", "Soil rolling after sowing: +2.5 % yield (base game)", "FS25 Official Manual (EN), Soil & Grass Rolling; GIANTS Ground Working 101 articles 291, 295, 318 (Nov 18, 2021, FS22)"},
    {"Rolling in North America", "Soybean", "Rolling before/after planting: no significant difference in stand, yield or seed quality (2008-2010 trials)", "U of Minnesota Extension, Rolling soybeans: the good, the bad and the injured"},
    {"Insurance - first season", "All insured crops", "Crops already planted when insurance first runs on a save can be covered once, before any damage", "Game rule (team) - not RMA"},
}
